# Reproduction supplement

canonical_input/ is the recovered immutable input tree. fresh_runs/canonical_01/ contains the new runner's code copies, logs and results. The pinned environment is requirements-reproduction.txt; the exact original command and all input/output hashes are in evidence/REPRODUCTION_ENVELOPE.json. To reproduce at another location, invoke canonical_input/computation/reproduce.py --all --historical --workdir NEW_EMPTY_RUN_DIRECTORY --timeout 180 using an environment with those versions. Do not rerun inside the archived source or retained run folders.

fresh_runs/paper_b_current_03 contains the complete current implementation snapshot and successful116-test command;01/02 preserve packaging failures. PAPER_B_TEST_ENVIRONMENT.json lists the separate project interpreter dependencies. No cloud calls were made by the selected tests.

p14_original/ contains completed frozen records, primary source scripts and manifest. p14_reconciliation/ contains the fresh arithmetic verification and inherited interpretation. These files support record verification, not a turnkey new timing campaign: the original timing harness has external source-repository paths, and new timings require their full separately retained runtime plus a new appropriate freeze/budget. The existing original runtime remains in CM_Computation/audit_p1_p13_20260918. No fresh holdout should be generated from this package as though it were unexposed data.

scripts/ retains exact execution scripts; original absolute paths are provenance and must be deliberately adjusted for a different machine. The canonical runner is relative-root aware. The artifact manifest lists the exact bytes included here. No native research database, virtual environment or credentials are included.
